// O04-B08 — the one additional declared callee premise the routes-mask arm
// traverses once aggregate stores stop refusing before the contract in force is
// consulted. Concatenated onto `o04_path.qcore` and `o04_arms_callees.qcore`,
// both of which stay byte-unchanged so cards O04 and O04-ARMS keep their exact
// premise sets.
//
// EVERY declaration here is a TRUSTED ASSUMPTION. It is not derived from any
// body in this fixture and it is not offered as a production declaration: this
// file lives with the gateway test fixtures, so the pinned `contract/qcore`
// corpus count is untouched.
//
// Card O04-ARMS measured `flb_time_now` *inert* and deliberately left it
// undeclared, because its statement `ic->create_time = flb_time_now();` was an
// aggregate store that refused before any contract was consulted. This card
// admits that store, so the call is no longer inert and the measurement changes
// with it: without this declaration the routes-mask arm would report
// `call to uncontracted function `flb_time_now`` instead. That movement is
// recorded in the card report rather than hidden.
//
// `flb_trace` stays deliberately UNcontracted: it is on the success exit's path
// only, which is out of scope, and keeping it uncontracted keeps a real refusal
// in place there.

// Premise: reading the clock takes no argument and returns no custody.
extern fn flb_time_now() -> u64
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
